WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.069
-Joe Biden has been elected

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.537
the 46th President
in the United States

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.806
in a historic and overwhelming
repudiation of Donald Trump

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.242
that ended with
Rudy Giuliani screaming

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.810
outside a landscaping company.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.413
And now nearly
the entire Republican Party

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.980
is in lockstep behind Trump

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.550
as he tries to delegitimize
and steal the election.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.420
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.256 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:27.293
Well, our long national
acid trip is almost over,

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.062
and now it's time
to pop a Klonopin

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.263
and let our designated
driver take us home.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:33.132
On Saturday,
all the major networks

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.435
finally called the presidential
election for Joe Biden,

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.903
and I have to say,
even I'm surprised

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:40.306
at just how relieved I am
that we don't have to suffer

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.907
through another four years
of Donald Trump,

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:44.910
the single most annoying human
being on the face of the Earth.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.079
Even if you put aside
everything else about him --

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:50.016
the racism, venality, cruelty,
corruption, mendacity,

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.818
vindictiveness,
and flagrant disregard

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.719
for any life
other than his own,

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:57.257
he is still just a world-
historically irritating man,

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.958
and the most irritating thing
about him

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.626
was my and and many people's

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.229
absolute round-the-clock
inability to look away.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:06.098
For four years, it has been
genuinely necessary

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:09.502
to monitor the President
24 hours a day, like zoologists

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.405
staring at two endangered rhinos
hoping they'll have sex.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.041
I mean, can you imagine living
through another four years

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.843
of having to see his sweaty,
overcooked ham of a face

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.712
on your television every day --

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.247
whining about toilets
not flushing

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:24.250
or windmills killing birds,
barking at reporters on his lawn

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.452
like a Long Island
mattress store owner

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:28.087
who insists on doing
his own commercials

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.555
and putting all his weird,

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.724
asymmetrical adult children
in them?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.660
[ As Donald Trump ] "So come on
down to Oceanside Mattress

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.796
and use the promo code
'Shut Up And Lay Down.'"

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.397
[ Normal voice ] And thank God,
we won't have to

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.299
watch him dance
at his rallies anymore,

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.702
like the naked guy
in the gym locker room

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.638
using his a towel to dry
the back of his neck.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.807
This point...
[ Laughs ]

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.276
...in addition to preserving
what's left of our democracy,

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.578
reversing four years
of malicious racism,

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.180
savagery, and criminal neglect,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.783
getting rid of Trump is just
a quality-of-life issue,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.284
like calling 311

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.419
about a jackhammer
outside your apartment.

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:03.189
And clearly, I'm not the only
one indulging myself

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.757
in the joy and catharsis
of seeing

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.960
this deeply wretched husk
of a man thrown out on his ass.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.762
As the results came in
over the last few days --

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.597
culminating with
the official call

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.266
from the networks
on Saturday --

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.968
there were celebrations
across the country,

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.336
with people dancing
in the streets,

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.938
honking, and banging pots
in New York City,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.374
flipping off Trump's
motorcade in D.C.,

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.575
dressing up as mailboxes
in Philadelphia,

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:25.345
and trolling Trump by blasting
what has become

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:28.047
his campaign's theme music --
the "YMCA" song.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:31.818
-♪ It's fun to stay
at the YMCA ♪

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.453
♪ It's fun to stay at the ♪

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.288
-♪ YMCA! ♪

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.324
-It's just fantastic,
and I love they're doing it

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.425
right outside the White House.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.960
It's like playing
"New York, New York"

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.462
outside of Fenway Park.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.196
I like to imagine that while
this was happening,

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:47.733
there was a also a sad flotilla
of Trump's beautiful boaters

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.670
mournfully circling the waters
off Clearwater Beach

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.472
to a funeral-dirge version
of "YMCA."

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.575
"Why, God, why...

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.809
M-C-A."

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.111
Dancing crowds weren't
the only people overjoyed

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:01.547
by the fact that we'll soon be
rid of Donald Trump.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.117
It was Joe Biden himself
who came bounding out

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.452
for his victory speech
like a journeyman reliever

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.753
jogging out from the bullpen

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.156
after finally getting called
up to the big leagues.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.058
It's nice to get Quaid
from "The Rookie"

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.527
after four years of Quaid
from "Total Recall."

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:17.063
-[ Screaming ]

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.164
-I know in one case,
it's the actor's name,

00:03:19.164 --> 00:03:20.732
and in the other,
it's the character's name,

00:03:20.732 --> 00:03:22.135
but the joke is
for Andy Samberg,

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.636
and I'm pretty sure he's gonna
like it just fine.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.337
Anyway, I think we can all admit

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:28.274
that when we were watching
Biden jog out,

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.142
we were silently hoping
he wouldn't fall.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.612
Anytime a 77-year-old man
exerts himself like that,

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:34.747
it's a white-knuckle ride.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.548
Biden's definitely
one of those grandpas

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:38.484
who insists on doing
everything himself.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.285
"Grandpa, it's 5:00 in the
morning. Where are you going?"

00:03:40.285 --> 00:03:42.921
"I'm gonna shovel the sidewalk
before my back pills wear off."

00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:45.058
And then, Biden spoke
for the first time

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:49.128
as President-Elect, and I mean
this in the best possible way --

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.096
I remember very little of it.

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:54.000
Like, I think he said stuff
about healing our divides

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.534
or unifying the country --
or whatever.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:58.237
Honestly, I'm just relieved
that a President-Elect

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.706
spoke to the nation
and I didn't immediately Google

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:02.374
"Canada how move to."

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:04.944
And then, Today, Biden announced
a task force of experts

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.079
who will guide him in dealing
with the coronavirus pandemic,

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.280
which, let's not forget,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.683
is currently ravaging
the country uncontrolled,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.918
with ICUs filling up

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.387
and hospitalizations
nearing record levels.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.522
And yet, as the crisis was
continuing to spiral,

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.692
the current President was moping
around his private golf course,

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.960
like a Palm Beach dentist
after a messy divorce.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.663
And that's also where Trump was
when the race was called

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:26.765
for Biden on Saturday,
which is just perfect.

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:29.001
Surprised he didn't
just stay out there.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.336
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
"Just leave me here.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.871
I live with the geese now."

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:34.374
[ Normal voice ] I wonder if
his aides gave him the news

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.008
out on the course
or waited until he got back.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.443
If I were them, I'd wait until

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.212
he doesn't have
a golf club in his hand.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.847
Can you imagine the rage divots
he left behind?

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:44.049
It's probably why Rudy Giuliani
always looks like that.

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:45.317
He gave Trump
some bad news once,

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.419
and there's still a 9-iron
wedged up his ass.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:50.523
So, clearly, Biden supporters
and sane people everywhere

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.858
got to enjoy a well-earned
national moment of catharsis

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:54.293
as the results came in.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:55.661
Now, let's check in
on the other side

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.063
and see how they're
taking the news.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.198
-President Trump
should not concede.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.199
-It was stolen.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.668
-The media is desperately trying

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:07.306
to get everyone to coronate
Joe Biden as the next president.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.976
-I think he would
have to do a lot

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.743
to convince Republicans

00:05:11.743 --> 00:05:14.981
that this is anything
except a left-wing power grab

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.982
financed by people
like George Soros.

00:05:16.982 --> 00:05:20.586
I think that it is
a corrupt, stolen election.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.022
-There is no Joe Biden.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.724
The man you may remember
from the 1980s is gone.

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:27.526
He no longer exists.

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:29.595
What remains is
a projection of sorts,

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.630
a hologram designed
to mimic the behavior

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.599
of a non-threatening
political candidate.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.968
These people seek
absolute sameness,

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.803
total uniformity.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.006
You're happy with
your corner coffee shop.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.741
They want to make you drink
Starbucks every day

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:46.278
from now until forever,
no matter how it tastes.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:48.814
-"And when that hologram
drinks coffee,

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.316
what do you think happens?

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.251
Splashes right to the ground,

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.354
because holograms
don't have real stomachs."

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:56.555
Alright.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.891
So, based on the clips,
they're not doing great.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.260
Tucker Carlson thinks Joe Biden
is a hologram

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.328
who wants to make you
drink Starbucks every day.

00:06:03.328 --> 00:06:04.630
And I'm sorry, but when is

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.565
the "Starbucks for liberals"
myth gonna die?

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:09.101
Are we supposed to believe
Tucker only drinks

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:12.037
campfire coffee
out of a prospector's tin mug?

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:13.472
And, by the way,
to anyone who thought

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:15.374
things were gonna go back
to normal once Trump is gone,

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:18.211
just a reminder -- Fox News
called Biden a hologram

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.079
who wants to force you
to drink Starbucks,

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.947
and he's been President-Elect
for two days.

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.148
Can you imagine
what it's gonna be like

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:24.650
when Biden's actually in office

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.885
if Republicans hang on
to control of the Senate?

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.854
Who knows if they'll even
let him have a Cabinet?

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.123 line:0%
Sean Hannity will probably
accuse Biden of building

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:34.093 line:0%
a secret Soros-funded
Amtrak station on the moon.

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.260 line:0%
But you know what?

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.562
Say what you will
about Republicans --

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.865
one thing they make clear
is they're tough guys

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.633
who don't cry like liberals.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:43.168
So, if anyone can handle
a bruising emotional defeat

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:45.270
like this one,
it's the Republican Party.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.907
-This is one of the things --
just give people time.

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:50.542
-Yes.
-I mean, you know,

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:53.078
he's just found out
that he's probably not gonna be

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:54.413
the President
of the United States here.

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:56.114
And, I mean, you can say,
"Well, it was in the cards,"

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:57.817
but you don't know
until the votes are counted.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.219
-I believe in decency
in all matters,

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:01.787
and I think
the decent thing to do

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:05.857
is let the President himself
take the time he wants

00:07:05.857 --> 00:07:07.059
to absorb this.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.729
It is not easy, and it is
extraordinarily close.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:12.331
So if the President
needs to take a few days --

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.666
maybe even longer -- to absorb,

00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:17.769
ultimately, accept --
and I think he ultimately will

00:07:17.769 --> 00:07:19.538
accept the outcome
of the people --

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.841
you have to
allow that to happen.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:22.842
-Truly incredible.

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:24.109
The "liberal tears" crowd --

00:07:24.109 --> 00:07:25.344
the people who spent four years

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:27.046
building an entire
political movement

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:29.081
around triggering
their political opponents

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.316
need a warm blanket
and a cup of Earl Grey tea

00:07:31.316 --> 00:07:33.118
to cope with losing
a presidential election.

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:36.989
They literally wore shirts that
said "[Bleep] your feelings."

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.692
"Yes, [bleep] your feelings,
but my feelings?

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:43.229
You make love to my feelings."

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.698
But this isn't just a case of
hurt feelings or wounded egos.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.332
This is the beating heart
of Trumpism --

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:49.401
the paranoid,
authoritarian belief

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:51.070
that your political opponents
are illegitimate.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.772
And even though Trump himself
might be on his way out,

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:55.808
the deep rot
that the rise has exposed

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.376
within our political system

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:58.744
isn't going anywhere
anytime soon,

00:07:58.744 --> 00:07:59.979
and we can't pretend otherwise.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:02.515
It runs through the veins
of the Republican Party,

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:04.583
which is why Trump
was thoroughly

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:05.917
and overwhelmingly repudiated.

00:08:05.917 --> 00:08:08.020
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris
won the most votes

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.889
for any presidential
ticket ever

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.124
and by one of the largest
margins in recent history.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:15.560
They're on pace to potentially
win over 300 electoral votes.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.629
Meanwhile, Trump is the
only president in history

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:19.498
to be impeached,
lose the popular vote,

00:08:19.498 --> 00:08:20.632
and be denied a second term.

00:08:20.632 --> 00:08:22.767
He's gonna be the answer
to a trivia question

00:08:22.767 --> 00:08:23.902
for the rest of his life.

00:08:23.902 --> 00:08:26.004
"Oh, man, I know this one.
Guy used to --

00:08:26.004 --> 00:08:27.239
His name was on buildings!

00:08:27.239 --> 00:08:29.942
Aaagh! You know -- golf guy!
Aah!

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:32.044
I knew I shouldn't have gotten
stoned before trivia night."

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:33.211
Again, Trump is not unique.

00:08:33.211 --> 00:08:35.214
For example, last night,
he retweeted a clip

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:37.083
from Fox News
in which Ken Starr,

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:39.017
the special prosecutor from
the Clinton impeachment,

00:08:39.017 --> 00:08:42.255
suggested that counting votes
was itself illegal.

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:45.758
-To count every vote
may be a crime.

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:48.527
[ Laughs ] It may even be
a crime under federal law.

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:51.596
It's definitely a crime
under state law if that is --

00:08:51.596 --> 00:08:54.734
and here's the key word --
illegal.

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:57.736
And that's why you see --
and it's shameful

00:08:57.736 --> 00:09:01.507
that Vice President Biden's
people

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:05.544
and the Vice President himself
are saying "Count every vote"

00:09:05.544 --> 00:09:07.679
and selling a lot of T-shirts.

00:09:07.679 --> 00:09:09.615
-Okay, putting aside
everything else for a second,

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:11.884
you're mad that
they're selling T-shirts?

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.886
All Trump does is sell
and advertise

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:15.153
Trump-branded products.

00:09:15.153 --> 00:09:17.256
The entire Trump campaign
is like the merch table

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.457
outside a concert.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:21.160
They have hats, shirts,
cups, flags.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.963
There's even an official
Trump/Pence pet leash,

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:26.698
which just seems
way too on-the-nose.

00:09:26.698 --> 00:09:28.400
[ Imitating Mike Pence ]
"Mr. President, I would prefer

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.636
if we didn't have
the leash on the website."

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:32.171
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
"Oh, you know, I hear you, Mike,

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:34.006
and I'm gonna take that
under consideration

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:38.344
right after you fetch
this [bleep] ball for me!"

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:39.745
[ Normal voice ]
But I appreciate Ken Starr

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:42.514
revealing the ideological core
of the Republican Party --

00:09:42.514 --> 00:09:45.151
their fundamental belief that
counting every vote is a crime.

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:47.686
They believe the democratic
process is illegitimate.

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:49.989
That's why they're manufacturing
deranged fantasies

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:51.924
of systemic voter fraud
without evidence.

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:54.326
Even when pressed for evidence,
they can't provide any.

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:59.965 line:0%
-I know this city has
a sad history of voter fraud.

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:04.670 line:0%
After all, Joe Frazier
is still voting here.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.872 line:0%
Kind of hard since he died
five years ago,

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:09.108 line:0%
but Joe continues to vote.

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:11.643 line:0%
If I recall correctly,
Joe was a Republican,

00:10:11.643 --> 00:10:13.612 line:0%
so maybe I shouldn't complain,

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.181 line:0%
but we should go see
if Joe is voting

00:10:15.181 --> 00:10:18.084 line:0%
Republican or Democrat now
from the grave.

00:10:18.084 --> 00:10:19.719 line:0%
In Philadelphia,

00:10:19.719 --> 00:10:22.054 line:0%
they keep the votes
of dead people secret.

00:10:22.054 --> 00:10:24.089
-Anytime Rudy does
a press conference,

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:26.325
I half expect him to be trailed
by an IV stand

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.593
and a nurse holding
a little cup full of pills.

00:10:28.593 --> 00:10:31.029
One of these days, he's gonna be
interrupted halfway through

00:10:31.029 --> 00:10:33.599
by an orderly yelling,
"Rudy! There you are!

00:10:33.599 --> 00:10:36.302
Free time is o--
It's lights-out at 8:00, Rudy!"

00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:39.471
[ Imitating Rudy Giuliani ] "I'm
making some very good points!

00:10:39.471 --> 00:10:41.907
Can I finish making my --
They're very good points!"

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:43.408
[ Normal voice ]
Gets crazier, though,

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:45.410
because that's the same press
conference where Rudy found out

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.246
the networks had all
called the race for Trump,

00:10:48.246 --> 00:10:49.481
and this was his response.

00:10:49.481 --> 00:10:50.983 line:0%
-Who was it called by?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.785 line:0%
All the --
Oh, my goodness!

00:10:53.785 --> 00:10:55.587 line:0%
All the networks!

00:10:55.587 --> 00:10:57.023 line:0%
Wow!

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.892 line:0%
All the networks!

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:02.194
-You know, Rudy doesn't think
it's official

00:11:02.194 --> 00:11:05.397
until it's called
by the "Texaco Star Theater."

00:11:05.397 --> 00:11:06.432
Sounds like he's on the phone

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:07.866
with Time Warner
customer service.

00:11:07.866 --> 00:11:09.768
"Alright, sir, we have
several packages available.

00:11:09.768 --> 00:11:11.003
Which channels would you like?"

00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:12.705 line:0%
-All the networks!

00:11:12.705 --> 00:11:14.773
-[ Laughs ] But by far,
the best thing

00:11:14.773 --> 00:11:17.542
about this press conference
was not what Rudy said,

00:11:17.542 --> 00:11:18.811
but where he said it.

00:11:18.811 --> 00:11:21.880
It brings us to the
absolutely top part of the week,

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.949
and, honestly, it was
almost as good as Trump losing.

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:26.451
You see, the way we found out
about this press conference

00:11:26.451 --> 00:11:27.520
was when Trump tweeted

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.554
"Lawyers news conference,
Four Seasons,

00:11:29.554 --> 00:11:31.556
Philadelphia, 11:00 A.M.,"
and then he deleted that tweet

00:11:31.556 --> 00:11:33.058
and followed up with another,
that said,

00:11:33.058 --> 00:11:34.659
"Big press conference today
in Philadelphia

00:11:34.659 --> 00:11:38.263
at Four Seasons
Total Landscaping, 11:30 a.m."

00:11:38.263 --> 00:11:40.132
So, everyone thought they were
holding a press conference

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:41.633
at the upscale
Four Seasons Hotel,

00:11:41.633 --> 00:11:43.169
and it turned out
they were holding it

00:11:43.169 --> 00:11:45.737
at a landscaping company called
Four Seasons Total Landscaping,

00:11:45.737 --> 00:11:47.639
and the hotel itself announced
they had no connection

00:11:47.639 --> 00:11:49.942
to either Trump
or the landscaping company.

00:11:49.942 --> 00:11:52.644
It's like if Trump announced
he was holding a big rally

00:11:52.644 --> 00:11:55.046
at the Lincoln Memorial,
deleted it, then announced

00:11:55.046 --> 00:11:57.750
he was holding a big rally
at a Lincoln dealership.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.451
So, how did this absolutely
incredible moment

00:11:59.451 --> 00:12:00.519
in history happen?

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:02.254
The Trump team
was reportedly looking

00:12:02.254 --> 00:12:04.489
for a friendly part of town
to hold the press conference,

00:12:04.489 --> 00:12:06.759
where they wouldn't get
drowned out by Biden supporters.

00:12:06.759 --> 00:12:08.360
But according to
The New York Times,

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:09.962
"Aides told the President
on Saturday morning

00:12:09.962 --> 00:12:11.629
their intended location
for the news conference,

00:12:11.629 --> 00:12:15.800
and he misunderstood, assuming
it was an upscale hotel."

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.069
But I think it was even dumber.

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:18.770
I think Trump said,
"Do it at the Four Seasons,"

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:20.205
and one of his
chucklehead henchmen

00:12:20.205 --> 00:12:22.607
just glanced at the Philly
phonebook, saw "Four Seasons,"

00:12:22.607 --> 00:12:24.877
dialed the number before he saw
"Total Landscaping,"

00:12:24.877 --> 00:12:26.211
and they just rolled with it

00:12:26.211 --> 00:12:27.713
because nobody
can admit a mistake

00:12:27.713 --> 00:12:29.781
in that fake
macho basement cult.

00:12:29.781 --> 00:12:30.850
It's just the best.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.184
He thought he was getting
a fancy hotel,

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:34.052
and instead, he got
a landscaping company.

00:12:34.052 --> 00:12:36.321
Something tells me
this isn't the first time

00:12:36.321 --> 00:12:37.522
this has happened to Rudy.

00:12:37.522 --> 00:12:39.724
if you've ever seen him
sleeping in a courtyard,

00:12:39.724 --> 00:12:41.926
It's because he thought
he was booking a room

00:12:41.926 --> 00:12:43.462
at Courtyard by Marriott.

00:12:43.462 --> 00:12:45.030
[ Imitating Giuliani ] "These
benches are so comfortable!

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.798
When's the turnover service?

00:12:46.798 --> 00:12:49.268
Plus, they have
all the networks!"

00:12:49.268 --> 00:12:50.903
[ Normal voice ] And it just
keeps getting better

00:12:50.903 --> 00:12:53.272
once you learn what else was
near the landscaping company.

00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:55.106
Again, this is where
the President's lawyer

00:12:55.106 --> 00:12:56.508
held an official
press conference

00:12:56.508 --> 00:12:59.544
falsely alleging a scheme
of wide-scale voter fraud

00:12:59.544 --> 00:13:01.380
